### How to build your trees
- **No worktree is created in the NexusAI repo, and you never work in its `2_Project_Files` checkout or any builder `worktrees/` directory** (S86M's `worktrees/s86m-rd618`, `worktrees/s86m-rd735`). In that repo use ONLY read verbs: `show`, `diff`, `log`, `ls-tree`, `cat-file`, `grep`, `ls-remote`, `rev-parse`, `merge-base`, `rev-list` (plus `count-objects` for §7.9). **NEVER `fetch`, `pull`, `push`, `checkout`, `worktree`, `commit`, `stash`, `gc`, `merge`; and `merge-tree --write-tree` ONLY with `GIT_OBJECT_DIRECTORY=<your own scratch dir> GIT_ALTERNATE_OBJECT_DIRECTORIES=<repo>/.git/objects`.**
- **Every tree is K1** — `git clone --shared --no-checkout <repo> <dir>` then `checkout` in YOUR clone (origin removed; local identity; `gc.auto 0`; `core.fsmonitor false`; hooks off), under a fresh `mktemp -d` in `/Volumes/KK_T9_External_HDD/!CODING/Testing Agent MAIN/projects/nexusai/qa-trees/batch16.XXXXXX/`. Status-check before use.
- **Each tree is EXCLUSIVE to this gate and to ONE purpose.** A fresh arm per mutant; never reuse a mutant tree for a clean arm; `batch16`-prefixed directories only. **Gates 14's and 15's trees (`qa-trees/batch14.*`, `qa-trees/batch15.*`) are LIVE peers' — never run in them, never write to them, never clone node_modules FROM them** (nor from gate 12's or 13's).
- **The red-at-parent tree:** YOUR clone at `953a0e6` with ONLY the server entry point restored to **`a938930`** (`fd01298`'s), hashed after the restore and committed IN YOUR CLONE ONLY so it is a clean K1. **The fd01298 tree:** YOUR clone at `fd01298` (for m5's side-by-side local run and m10).
- **`node_modules` — ONE lockfile (`e9063d4`).** Each tree runs on node_modules PROVEN for it (`npm ls --all --offline` rc 0; every `invalid`/`extraneous`/`missing` line quoted; axios, http-cache-semantics, sqlite3 read back). **Source (H-31):** ONCE, `npm ci --offline --ignore-scripts --no-audit --no-fund --cache "<your mktemp dir>/npm-cache"` in YOUR OWN K1 tree, the `_cacache` an APFS clone (`cp -c -R`) of `~/.npm/_cacache`; **then sqlite3's binding from an APFS clone of `~/.npm/_prebuilds` by sqlite3's own `prebuild-install` inside the strict belt, the log saying "found cached prebuild … unpacking", and a load proof** (ruling m, its three conditions). An `ENOTCACHED` is NOT RUN for that tree — name it and mail a QUESTION; **never go online.** Every other tree gets node_modules by an APFS clone of YOUR proven tree. A real directory, never a symlink. **Never `npm install`.** Say that `--ignore-scripts` differs from CI's form (L-Y1).

